              <h3 class="offcanvas-title">Symbiota</h3>
              <button type="button" class="btn-close" aria-label="Close"></button>
            </div>
            <div class="offcanvas-body p-0">
              <div class="list-group list-group-flush">
                <h5 class="dropdown-header">Organisation</h5>
                <a class="list-group-item list-group-item-action" href="#components"><i class="bi bi-pencil"></i> Edit</a>
                <a class="list-group-item list-group-item-action" href="#components"><i class="bi bi-people"></i> Members</a>
                <hr class="my-1">
                <a class="list-group-item list-group-item-action" href="#components"><i class="bi bi-ticket"></i> Orders</a>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="spec">Below 768px, nav crumbs scroll sideways like tabs, with the same edge fades and chevrons, and they (dropdown_nav, ul_nav), the notifications and messages dropdowns open in #nav-dropdown-sheet (layouts/application.erb) in place of a dropdown: an offcanvas-bottom as tall as its content up to 80dvh, its top corners --bs-border-radius-xl · app.js copies the menu in as a list-group-flush with no borders, headers as .dropdown-header with no line, as in nav crumbs, dividers as an hr · the event stats row opens in it too, as a list of its columns</div>
      <% end %>
    </div>

    <% design_subsection 'Date and icon tiles', 'The event page\'s date, location and link, as tiles beside the details they stand for. On the site they\'re CSS (.event-detail in app.css, over event_details.css): white, a --hairline border, --bs-box-shadow-sm, .3em corners, 2.5em square; the month a bold, letter-spaced band of --theme-50 in --theme-800 over a semibold day; icons 1.5em in black at 50%. On hover the tile turns solid theme. Emails can\'t rely on that CSS, so they show the same tiles as PNGs from <code>rake icons:generate</code> (app/views/icons), at 2.75em with the tile inset to match: the month band green for the default theme, grey for events and organisations with their own colour (the location and camera tiles are the same in both).'.html_safe do %>
      <% today = Date.today; png_date = "#{today.strftime('%b').downcase}_#{today.strftime('%d')}" %>
      <div class="row g-4">
        <div class="col-lg-6">
          <%# events/_details.erb, as on the event page, for the sample event (@event while it renders) %>
          <% event_was, @event = @event, design_sample_event %>
          <%= partial :'events/details', locals: { n: 1, events: [@event] } %>
          <% @event = event_was %>
          <div class="spec">Site: .event-detail.calendar-date, .event-detail.location (or the camera for online events) and .event-detail.link · hover one</div>
        </div>
        <div class="col-lg-6">
          <% { 'green' => 'Default theme', 'greyscale' => 'Own theme colour' }.each do |scheme, label| %>
            <div class="d-flex align-items-center gap-2 mb-2" style="font-size: 1.1em">
              <% ["calendar/png/#{scheme}/#{png_date}", "image/#{scheme}/image-camera-video", "image/#{scheme}/image-geo-alt"].each do |path| %>
                <img src="/images/icons/<%= path %>.png" alt="" style="width: 2.75em">
              <% end %>
              <span class="small text-body-secondary ms-2"><%= label %></span>
            </div>
          <% end %>
          <div class="spec mt-3">Email: 160px PNGs in app/assets/images/icons/calendar/png and icons/image, picked by emails/_tickets_table.erb</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    <% end %>

    <% design_subsection 'Event block', 'How events are listed on organisation and search pages (events/_block.erb, with _block_main.erb). From 992px the image sits on the right, filling its half (cropped when the text is taller), and the row is a white card with a --hairline border, base radius and --bs-box-shadow-sm; below that the image stacks on top.' do %>
      <%# Rendered as on its organisation's events page, so its Featured label shows %>
      <% organisation_was, @organisation = @organisation, design_sample_event.organisation %>
      <%= partial :'events/block', locals: { event: design_sample_event, skip_pagelets: true } %>
      <% @organisation = organisation_was %>
      <div class="spec">Name h2 · labels: Featured text-bg-yellow, Sold out or Sales ended text-bg-danger, Locked text-bg-secondary · tags text-bg-primary, up to 5, with bi-stars when AI-tagged · .icon-list at fs-4, each line's icon hung 2em to the left, with a tooltip naming it</div>
    <% end %>

    <% design_subsection 'Tiles', 'How organisations, gatherings and activities are listed (_block.erb, from organisations/, gatherings/ and activities/_blocks.erb): two to a row, then four from 992px, each 10rem high.' do %>
      <% sample_image = design_sample_image %>
      <% check = '<i data-bs-toggle="tooltip" title="Gratitude for financially supporting the Dandelion platform 🙏" class="bi bi-patch-check-fill"></i>' %>
      <div class="row">
        <% [
             { title: 'Breathwork Collective', image: sample_image },
             { title: 'Mira Khanya - Movement Medicine', image: nil, icon: check },
             { title: 'The Way Forward: Awakened and Embodied Feminine Leadership Gathering - October 12th–14th', image: nil },
             { title: 'Embercombe', image: sample_image, icon: check }
           ].each do |tile| %>
          <div class="col-6 col-lg-3 mb-3">
            <%= partial :block, locals: { title: tile[:title], image: tile[:image], icon: tile[:icon], view_url: '#components', admin: false } %>
          </div>
        <% end %>
      </div>
      <div class="spec">The whole tile links through the title's .stretched-link; hovered or keyboard focused, it takes --bs-box-shadow and a photo's black eases to 40% · title .block-title: --font-size-xl, clamped to 4 lines, so a line is always left empty at the bottom; long words break · with an image: the photo under black at 50%, white text · without: .block-fill, the lavender wash (lavender-50 to paper) with a --hairline border, dark text · an icon such as the verified tick follows the title after a &amp;nbsp;, so it keeps to the line with its last word · admins get a pencil on hover, and activities a link to their organisation at the bottom right</div>
    <% end %>

    <% design_subsection 'Carousel', 'Featured events and the organisation\'s own carousels (upcoming events, plus past ones with recordings) on organisation pages (events/_carousel.erb), with Slick: three to a slide from 992px, two from 576px, then one.' do %>
      <div class="slick-container" id="dg-slick">
        <div class="slick-responsive row justify-content-center">
          <%# The slides are events/_block_carousel.erb; the wrapper is _carousel.erb's, which caches each slide by event id %>
          <% saturday = Date.today.next_occurring(:saturday) %>
          <% [design_sample_event,
              design_build_event('Sound bath', day: saturday + 1, sold_out_cache: true),
              design_build_event('Breathwork weekend retreat', day: saturday + 6, days: 2),
              design_build_event('Ecstatic dance', day: saturday + 11),
              design_build_event('Breathwork foundations course', evergreen: true)].each do |event| %>
            <div class="col-12 col-sm-6 col-lg-4 slick-item">
              <%= partial :'events/block_carousel', locals: { event: event } %>
            </div>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </div>
      <script>
        $(function () {
          $('#dg-slick .slick-responsive').slick({
            speed: 300,
            dots: true,
            prevArrow: "<button type='button' class='rounded-circle slick-prev float-start'><i class='bi bi-chevron-compact-left'></i></button>",
            nextArrow: "<button type='button' class='rounded-circle slick-next float-end'><i class='bi bi-chevron-compact-right'></i></button>",
            slidesToShow: 3,
            slidesToScroll: 3,
            responsive: [{ breakpoint: 992, settings: { slidesToShow: 2, slidesToScroll: 2 } }, { breakpoint: 576, settings: { slidesToShow: 1, slidesToScroll: 1 } }]
          })
        })
      </script>
      <div class="spec">Arrows: 2.5rem white circles with black bi-chevron-compact icons, the whole button at 50% opacity, 75% on hover · dates and Sold out as .badge-overlay (see Badges) · before Slick loads, only the first item shows</div>
    <% end %>

    <% design_subsection 'Ticket purchase form', 'The Select tickets card on an event page (purchase/_purchase.erb), one row per ticket type from purchase/_ticket_type.erb, then discounts, a donation and the total down the right-hand column. Shown here without purchase.js, so totals don\'t add up.' do %>
      <div class="row g-5">
        <div class="col-lg-7">
          <div class="card" id="select-tickets">
            <h3 class="card-header text-bg-primary">Select tickets</h3>
            <div class="card-body" id="ticket-types">
              <table class="table mb-0">
                <% [
                     { group: 'Weekend', name: 'Standard', price: '£22', qty: true },
                     { name: 'Solidarity', price: '£8', qty: true, left: 2, description: 'For those on a low income. No questions asked.' },
                     { group: 'Day passes', name: 'Pay what you can', range: [5, 30], qty: true },
                     { name: 'Early bird', price: '£15', sold_out: true }
                   ].each do |t| %>
                  <% if t[:group] %>
                    <tr><td colspan="3" class="ticket-group-heading"><%= t[:group] %></td></tr>
                  <% end %>
                  <tr><td class="py-0 border-top" colspan="3"></td></tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td class="border-top-0 align-middle">
                      <span class="ticket-type-name fw-bold"><%= t[:name] %></span>
                      <% if t[:left] %><span class="badge text-bg-secondary align-text-bottom"><%= t[:left] %> left</span><% end %>
                    </td>
                    <td class="border-top-0 align-middle ticket-type-price">
                      <% if t[:range] %>
                        <span>£<%= t[:range].first %> - £<%= t[:range].last %></span>
                        <input type="range" class="form-range" min="<%= t[:range].first %>" max="<%= t[:range].last %>" autocomplete="off" aria-label="Price" oninput="$(this).prev().html('£' + this.value); $(this).next().find('.select-a-price-first').css('visibility', 'hidden')">
                        <div class="text-end small"><em class="select-a-price-first text-nowrap">Drag<span class="d-none d-sm-inline"> the slider</span></em></div>
                      <% else %>
                        <%= t[:price] %>
                      <% end %>
                    </td>
                    <td class="border-top-0 align-middle">
                      <% if t[:sold_out] %>
                        <div class="text-end"><button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-primary">Join waitlist</button></div>
                      <% else %>
                        <select class="form-select w-100" aria-label="Quantity"><% 0.upto(10) do |n| %><option><%= n %></option><% end %></select>
                      <% end %>
                    </td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr><td class="text-body-secondary ticket-type-description border-0 pt-0<% unless t[:description] %> pb-0<% end %>" colspan="3"><div><% if t[:description] %><p><%= t[:description] %></p><% end %></div></td></tr>
                <% end %>
                <tr>
                  <td></td>
                  <td></td>
                  <td>
                    <strong>Apply a code</strong>
                    <div class="input-group my-1">
                      <input type="text" class="form-control" style="width: 5em" autocomplete="off" aria-label="Code">
                      <button class="btn btn-outline-secondary" type="button">Apply</button>
                    </div>
                  </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td></td>
                  <td></td>
                  <td>
                    <strong>Add a donation to Dandelion</strong>
                    <div>
                      <div class="btn-group mt-1" id="donation-percent-buttons">
                        <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">1%</button>
                        <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-secondary active">5%</button>
                        <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">10%</button>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="input-group my-1">
                      <span class="input-group-text">£</span>
                      <input type="number" class="form-control" style="width: 5em" autocomplete="off" value="1.10" aria-label="Donation">
                    </div>
                  </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td></td>
                  <td></td>
                  <td style="min-width: 8em">
                    <strong>Total</strong>
                    <div class="input-group my-1">
                      <span class="input-group-text">£</span>
                      <input type="number" class="form-control" style="width: 5em" value="23.10" disabled autocomplete="off" aria-label="Total">
                    </div>
                  </td>
                </tr>
              </table>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col-lg-5 d-flex flex-column gap-3">
          <div class="bg-body-tertiary rounded p-4">
            <div class="modal position-static d-block h-auto overflow-visible" style="z-index: auto">
              <div class="modal-dialog my-0" style="width: auto">
                <div class="modal-content">
                  <div class="modal-header">
                    <h3 class="modal-title">Join waitlist</h3>
                    <button type="button" class="btn-close" aria-label="Close"></button>
                  </div>
                  <div class="modal-body">
                    <div class="mb-3">
                      <label for="dg-waitlist-name">Name</label>
                      <input type="text" class="form-control" id="dg-waitlist-name" autocomplete="off" value="Maya">
                    </div>
                    <div class="mb-0">
                      <label for="dg-waitlist-email">Email</label>
                      <input type="email" class="form-control" id="dg-waitlist-email" autocomplete="off" value="maya@example.com">
                    </div>
                  </div>
                  <div class="modal-footer">
                    <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary">Cancel</button>
                    <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary">Join waitlist</button>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="spec">Ticket groups: a .ticket-group-heading row, a bold 1.25rem heading, its group's first divider a 2px rule in --bs-emphasis-color · each type: the name bold at --font-size-base (.ticket-type-name), a lock icon if it's secret or for members, "3 left" or fewer as a text-bg-secondary badge · price at the same --font-size-base (.ticket-type-price), not bold: fixed, a form-range for a range (the price shows once dragged), or a £ input group for pay what you like, which enables the quantity · quantity a full-width form-select, 0 to 99, or to the number left if fewer · the description in --bs-secondary-color, its paragraphs without margin · sold out: Join waitlist (btn-sm btn-outline-primary), which opens the waitlist modal (purchase/_ticket_type_waitlist_modal.erb), or a Sold out badge in text-bg-danger, as in event blocks, the carousel and the places-filled bar · a ticket type whose sales have ended says Sales closed in text-bg-secondary · the right-hand column: Apply a code, a membership discount, the donation (1/5/10% of the total, 1/2.5/5% on large orders, or a set amount for the organisation) and the disabled Total, Credit, Discount and Balance fields from currency_input_row, each a bold label over a 5em input group · below 576px the card's sides narrow to .75rem, cells take table-sm's .5rem with none at the table's edges, and the range hint says just Drag, so the three columns fit a phone</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    <% end %>

    <div class="row g-5">
      <% design_subsection 'Comments', col: 'col-lg-7' do %>
        <div class="card">
          <h3 class="card-header text-bg-primary">Lift shares from London</h3>
          <div class="card-body p-0 pb-3">
            <% [['maya', 'Maya', '2 hours ago', "I'm driving down from Hackney on Friday morning, room for three. Message me!", [['💚', 4, true], ['🙏', 2, false]]],
                ['jonas', 'Jonas', '1 hour ago', 'Count me in, thank you @Maya', []]].each do |img, name, time, body, reactions| %>
              <div class="d-flex align-items-start m-0 px-2 pt-2">
                <span class="me-2"><img src="/images/samples/<%= img %>.jpg" alt="" class="avatar avatar-xs"></span>
                <div class="flex-grow-1 comment">
                  <strong><a href="#components"><%= name %></a></strong>
                  <small class="text-body-secondary"><%= time %></small>
                  <div class="mb-2"><div class="comment-body"><%= body %></div></div>
                  <div class="d-flex gap-1">
                    <% reactions.each do |emoji, count, mine| %>
                      <a href="#components" class="d-inline-block border rounded p-1 text-body text-decoration-none bg-white <%= mine ? 'border-primary' : 'border-light' %>"><% if emoji == '💚' %><i class="text-primary bi bi-heart-fill"></i><% else %><%= emoji %><% end %> <%= count %></a>
                    <% end %>
                    <a class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-primary" href="#components" data-bs-toggle="tooltip" title="React"><i class="bi bi-heart-fill"></i></a>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            <% end %>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="spec">A post (comments/_post.erb) is a card with a text-bg-primary header, its subject · each comment: an avatar-xs, the name bold, the time in --bs-secondary-color, the body linkified · reactions bordered tiles, your own bordered --theme-500, with the reactors' names in a tooltip</div>
      <% end %>

      <% design_subsection 'Avatars', col: 'col-lg-5' do %>
        <div class="d-flex align-items-end flex-wrap gap-3">
          <% [['Maya Okoro', 'maya'], ['Jonas Berg', 'jonas'], ['Amara Nwosu', 'amara'], ['Maya Okoro', 'maya'], ['Jonas Berg', 'jonas']].each_with_index do |(name, photo), i| %>
            <% size = %i[xs sm md lg xl][i] %>
            <div class="text-center">
              <%= partial :'accounts/square', locals: { account: design_sample_account(name, photo, private: i == 2), size: size } %>
              <div class="spec mt-1"><%= size %><%= ' · private' if i == 2 %></div>
            </div>
          <% end %>
        </div>
        <div class="spec mt-3">Square (accounts/_square.erb), except the 1.75rem header avatar and the 1.5rem chat avatars, which are round: the account's thumbnail or Gravatar, with their name in a tooltip · a size class, from <code>size:</code> (:sm by default): xs 2rem in comments, sm 3.125rem in lists of people (the most common), md 4rem in message threads and map info windows, lg 4.6875rem for team and gathering members, xl 6.25rem in account rows, 2xl 9.375rem beside feedback quotes, fill to take its column's width · img.private at 50%, full on hover · .profile-photo, the large photo at the top of a profile or application: 12.5rem, framed in white</div>
      <% end %>
    </div>

    <div class="row g-5">
      <% design_subsection 'Upcoming birthdays', col: 'col-lg-6' do %>
        <div class="card">
          <h3 class="card-header chill">Upcoming birthdays</h3>
          <div class="card-body">
            <div class="mb-3">
              <% [['Maya Okoro', 'maya', 0], ['Jonas Berg', 'jonas', 1], ['Amara Nwosu', 'amara', 6]].each do |name, photo, days| %>
                <%= partial :'accounts/birthday', locals: { account: design_sample_account(name, photo, date_of_birth: Date.today + days - 30.years) } %>
              <% end %>
            </div>
            <a href="#components">All birthdays &rarr;</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="spec">The home page's card (accounts/_birthday.erb): an avatar-xs, the name, and the weekday and date small in --bs-secondary-color · on the right a badge from accounts/_birthday_when.erb, also used on /birthdays and a gathering's members: text-bg-yellow with a cake for today, text-bg-primary for tomorrow, text-bg-secondary for in n days</div>
      <% end %>
    </div>

    <div class="row g-5">
      <% design_subsection 'Ratings and feedback', col: 'col-lg-7' do %>
        <div class="border rounded p-4 d-flex flex-column gap-4">
          <div class="average-rating">
            4.8<small class="text-body-secondary">/5 from 36 ratings across 12 events</small>
            <div class="d-lg-inline"><% 5.times do %><i class="bi bi-star-fill"></i><% end %></div>
          </div>
          <div class="rating-breakdown mb-0">
            <div class="text-center">
              <div class="rating-breakdown-average">4.3</div>
              <%= partial :'event_feedbacks/stars', locals: { rating: 4 } %>
              <div class="small text-body-secondary">12 ratings</div>
            </div>
            <div class="rating-breakdown-bars">
              <% { 5 => 6, 4 => 4, 3 => 2, 2 => 0, 1 => 0 }.each do |stars, count| %>
                <div class="rating-breakdown-row">
                  <span><%= stars %><i class="bi bi-star-fill"></i></span>
                  <div class="progress" role="presentation"><div class="progress-bar" style="width: <%= (100.0 * count / 12).round %>%"></div></div>
                  <span class="text-body-secondary text-end"><%= count %></span>
                </div>
              <% end %>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="feedback-list">
            <% [['amara', 'Amara', 5, '2 days ago', true],
                [nil, 'Anonymous', 4, '5 days ago', false],
                ['jonas', 'Jonas', 3, '2 weeks ago', false]].each do |img, name, stars, time, quote| %>
              <article class="feedback-entry">
                <div class="d-flex align-items-center gap-2 mb-1">
                  <%= partial :'event_feedbacks/stars', locals: { rating: stars } %>
                  <small class="text-body-secondary"><%= time %></small>
                </div>
                <% if quote %>
                  <div class="readable mb-1">A beautiful, gentle evening. Maya held the space with such care.</div>
                <% end %>
                <div class="small">
                  <% if img %><a href="#components"><%= name %></a><% else %><%= name %><% end %> <span class="text-body-secondary">on</span> <a href="#components">Full moon gathering</a>
                </div>
                <% if quote %>
                  <div class="feedback-reply mt-2">
                    <div class="small fw-semibold mb-1"><i class="bi bi-reply-fill"></i> Symbiota replied</div>
                    <div class="readable read-more">Thank you so much for coming!<br>We loved having you, and we'll be running the next one at the end of the month, with a longer sound bath.</div>
                  </div>
                <% end %>
              </article>
            <% end %>
          </div>
          <div class="feedback-rating-panel text-center py-4 px-3">
            <label class="feedback-question-label d-block mb-1">Your star rating</label>
            <p class="small text-body-secondary mb-3">Your star rating is always public and contributes towards the host's average.</p>
            <div class="feedback-stars" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Star rating">
              <% 1.upto(5) do |i| %>
                <i class="bi bi-star-fill<%= ' chosen' if i <= 4 %>" data-rating="<%= i %>" aria-label="<%= i %> out of 5 stars"></i>
              <% end %>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="spec">.average-rating (event_feedbacks/_average_rating.erb): the average at --font-size-2xl, the count in --bs-secondary-color, a star per point, in facilitator info · public feedback (event_feedbacks/_event_feedbacks.erb) opens with .rating-breakdown (_rating_breakdown.erb): the average at --font-size-3xl, bold, over its stars and count, beside a bar per star level, 5 down to 1, its numbers in tabular figures so the stars line up, in --color-orange-400 on --bs-tertiary-bg, at most 20rem wide · then the list, one .feedback-entry per rating with a translucent hairline between: the stars (event_feedbacks/_stars.erb, all five, the ones not given as .star-off at 40% in --bs-tertiary-color) and the date in --bs-secondary-color, then the public answers at .readable, then who and which event in small text · no profile pictures: the name links to the profile, or for people who aren't publicly visible is abbreviated with no link, and anonymous feedback reads Anonymous · removed feedback at 50% reads Removed in place of its stars · the organisation's reply under its answers as .feedback-reply, a 0.25rem primary rule on the left, headed by a bi-reply-fill and who replied in semibold small text · .read-more (app.js) cuts a reply at its first line break and adds a Read more link at --font-size-xs, which shows the rest · the feedback form (event_feedbacks/build.erb, styled by event_feedbacks.css): five 2.75rem stars on a --bs-tertiary-bg panel, radius lg, --bs-gray-300 until chosen, then --color-orange-400 with .chosen</div>
      <% end %>

      <% design_subsection 'Image wall', col: 'col-lg-5' do %>
        <%= partial :'accounts/add', locals: { accounts: [['Maya Okoro', 'maya'], ['Jonas Berg', 'jonas'], ['Amara Nwosu', 'amara']].cycle.first(7).map { |name, photo| design_sample_account(name, photo) }, add_and_remove: false } %>
        <div class="spec">.image-wall: groups of people as avatars that wrap, --space-2xs between rows: who chose an option or is interested in an activity, team and gathering members, attendees, followers · on options, teams and rotas, a "Show names instead of pictures" link reloads them as names separated by middots</div>
      <% end %>
    </div>

    <% design_subsection 'Calendar', 'An organisation\'s events by month or as a list (events/_calendar.erb), with FullCalendar. Events are --theme-500, or in embeds the organisation\'s own colour, so the grid has one colour: today\'s circle and the events. Each has a tooltip with its location and time.' do %>
      <script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/fullcalendar/6.1.19/index.global.min.js"></script>
      <div id="calendar"></div>
      <script>
        $(function () {
          var d = function (day, hour) { var t = new Date(); return new Date(t.getFullYear(), t.getMonth(), day, hour) }
          new FullCalendar.Calendar(document.getElementById('calendar'), {
            initialView: 'dayGridMonth',
            headerToolbar: { left: 'today prev,next title', center: '', right: 'dayGridMonth,listMonth' },
            buttonText: { today: 'Today', month: 'Month', week: 'Week', list: 'List' },
            height: 'auto',
            events: [['Ecstatic dance', 4, 19], ['Breathwork', 9, 18], ['Sound bath', 9, 20], ['Community supper', 15, 19], ['Full moon gathering', 21, 20], ['Men\'s circle', 27, 19]].map(function (e) {
              return { title: e[0], start: d(e[1], e[2]), end: d(e[1], e[2] + 2), url: '#components', color: cssColor('var(--theme-500)') }
            }),
            eventDidMount: function (info) {
              $(info.el).tooltip({ title: '<strong>' + info.event.title + '</strong><br><i class="bi bi-geo-alt-fill"></i> London', html: true, placement: 'top', trigger: 'hover', container: 'body' })
            }
          }).render()
        })
      </script>
      <div class="spec">Day numbers and headings --bs-secondary-color, since FullCalendar makes them href-less anchors that would otherwise take the link colour · today's number white on a --theme-500 circle, with no day tint · toolbar buttons like .btn-secondary, the active view filled --theme-500 like the active pill · prev and next borderless · on mobile the title drops to --font-size-base and Today hides</div>
    <% end %>

    <div class="row g-5">
      <% design_subsection 'Timetable', col: 'col-lg-6' do %>
        <div class="row g-3">
          <% [['Morning yoga', 'Maya', '5'], ['Sharing circle', 'Sam', nil]].each do |name, by, img| %>
            <div class="col-sm-6">
              <div class="tactivity<%= ' tactivity-image' if img %>"<% if img %> style="--tactivity-image: url('/images/dandelions/<%= img %>.jpeg')"<% end %>>
                <div class="position-absolute" style="bottom: .5rem; left: .5rem">
                  <h3 class="mt-0 mb-0"><a href="#components"><%= name %></a></h3>
                  <span>by <a href="#components"><%= by %></a></span>
                </div>
                <div class="position-absolute" style="right: .5rem; bottom: .5rem">
                  <a href="#components"><i class="bi bi-pencil-fill"></i></a>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          <% end %>
        </div>
        <div class="spec">A gathering's activities (timetables/_tactivity.erb), dragged into a table-striped grid of times by spaces · 8rem tall, 16rem wide in the grid · white with a 2px --bs-body-color border and text · .tactivity-image takes the image from --tactivity-image, darkened by black at 50% under white text</div>
      <% end %>

      <% design_subsection 'Map markers', col: 'col-lg-6' do %>
        <div class="d-flex align-items-end flex-wrap gap-4">
          <% [['var(--color-green-500)', 'bi-person-fill', 'People'], ['var(--color-green-500)', 'bi-people-fill', 'Gatherings'], ['var(--color-red-400)', 'bi-calendar-event', 'Events'], ['var(--color-red-400)', 'bi-flag-fill', 'Organisations']].each do |color, icon, label| %>
            <div class="text-center">
              <span class="position-relative d-inline-block" style="width: 36px; height: 48px">
                <svg viewBox="-18 -48 36 48" width="36" height="48" aria-hidden="true"><path fill="<%= color %>" d="M0-48c-9.8 0-17.8 7.9-17.8 17.6C-17.8-14.9 0 0 0 0s17.8-14.9 17.8-30.4C17.8-40.1 9.8-48 0-48z"></path></svg>
                <i class="bi <%= icon %> position-absolute start-50 translate-middle-x text-white" style="top: 8px; font-size: 18px"></i>
              </span>
              <div class="spec mt-1"><%= label %></div>
            </div>
          <% end %>
          <% [['var(--color-green-500)', 8], ['var(--color-orange-500)', 42], ['var(--color-red-500)', 130]].each do |color, n| %>
            <div class="text-center">
              <span class="position-relative d-inline-flex align-items-center justify-content-center fw-bold text-white" style="width: 50px; height: 50px">
                <svg class="position-absolute top-0 start-0" viewBox="0 0 50 50" width="50" height="50" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="25" cy="25" r="25" fill="<%= color %>" fill-opacity=".4"></circle><circle cx="25" cy="25" r="20" fill="<%= color %>"></circle></svg>
                <span class="position-relative"><%= n %></span>
              </span>
              <div class="spec mt-1">cluster</div>
            </div>
          <% end %>
        </div>
        <div class="spec mt-3">Google Maps (map.js): map-icons pins in --color-green-500 (the default green, whatever the theme) for people and gatherings, --color-red-400 for events and organisations, each with its white Bootstrap icon · clusters --color-green-500, --color-orange-500, then --color-red-500 as they grow, each with a 40% halo, drawn as SVGs since MarkerClusterer takes an image, with white Plus Jakarta Sans counts · areas drawn in --color-orange-400, filled at 35%</div>
      <% end %>
    </div>

    <div class="row g-5">
      <% design_subsection 'Map info window', col: 'col-lg-5' do %>
        <div class="bg-body-tertiary rounded p-4">
          <div class="gm-style position-relative bg-white mx-auto" style="max-width: 20rem; padding: 12px; border-radius: 8px; box-shadow: 0 2px 7px 1px rgba(var(--bs-black-rgb), .3)">
            <button type="button" class="btn-close position-absolute top-0 end-0 m-2" aria-label="Close"></button>
            <div class="infowindow">
              <%= partial :'points/account', locals: { account: design_sample_account('Maya Okoro', 'maya', event_tag_names: %w[breathwork sound]) } %>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="spec">Clicking a marker loads /points/:model/:id into Google's InfoWindow, wrapped in .infowindow: a person (points/_account.erb, as here), an organisation or gathering, or an event as its block's text without the image (events/_block_main.erb as ul.map-event, list items at --font-size-sm) · Google draws the white box, its tail and the close button; app.css sets its font to Plus Jakarta Sans, sizes the close button and zeroes .row margins inside</div>
      <% end %>

      <% design_subsection 'Email previews', col: 'col-lg-7' do %>
        <div class="email-preview-iframe-container border rounded" style="height: 20rem">
          <iframe title="Email preview" srcdoc="<%= '<body style="margin: 0; padding: 2rem; font-family: sans-serif; background: #f6f6f6"><div style="max-width: 32rem; margin: 0 auto; background: #fff; padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 8px"><h2 style="margin-top: 0">Your tickets to Full moon gathering</h2><p>Thanks for booking, Maya. Your tickets are attached.</p></div></body>' %>"></iframe>
        </div>
        <div class="spec">.email-preview-iframe-container, on the ticket, reminder and feedback request email pages (events/ticket_email.erb and friends): the email rendered by its own route into a borderless iframe that fills the container, 80vh tall (20rem here)</div>
      <% end %>
    </div>

    <% design_subsection 'Cookie banner' do %>
      <%# z-index: auto, since as a flex item it would otherwise keep its 1100 and cover the header %>
      <div class="cookie-consent position-static" style="z-index: auto">
        <div class="cookie-consent__copy">
          <h2>Cookies on Dandelion</h2>
          <p>Dandelion requires a few necessary cookies. We only use other cookies if you allow them.</p>
          <p><a href="#components">Cookie policy</a> <span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span> <a href="#components">Privacy policy</a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="cookie-consent__settings">
          <div class="form-check mb-0"><input class="form-check-input" type="checkbox" id="dg-cookie-necessary" checked disabled><label class="form-check-label" for="dg-cookie-necessary">Necessary</label></div>
          <div class="form-check mb-0"><input class="form-check-input" type="checkbox" id="dg-cookie-analytics"><label class="form-check-label" for="dg-cookie-analytics">Analytics</label></div>
          <div class="form-check mb-0"><input class="form-check-input" type="checkbox" id="dg-cookie-marketing"><label class="form-check-label" for="dg-cookie-marketing">Marketing</label></div>
        </div>
        <div class="cookie-consent__actions">
          <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-primary">Save choices</button>
          <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary">Accept all</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="spec">layouts/_cookie_consent.erb, fixed 1rem from the bottom, up to 64rem wide · radius lg, --hairline border, --bs-box-shadow · Necessary only and Customise until Customise is pressed, which shows the choices (as here, .form-check checkboxes) and Save choices · one column on mobile, the buttons stretched</div>
    <% end %>

    <% design_subsection 'Empty states' do %>
      <div class="border rounded p-4"><p class="mb-0 text-body-secondary">No upcoming events</p></div>
      <div class="spec">A short "No …" phrase in --bs-secondary-color, left-aligned and without a full stop, where the list or table would be: grey, since it is the absence of content rather than content</div>
    <% end %>

    <% design_subsection 'p.action', "A centred call to action for docs and email previews, where a .btn class can't be added. Drawn like btn-primary; emails use their own in email.css." do %>
      <div class="border rounded p-4">
        <p class="action m-0"><a href="#components">Confirm your email</a></p>
      </div>
    <% end %>

    <% design_subsection 'AI well and ask box', "The AI well is the only sheen, so the gradient itself marks AI: 135°, <code>--ai-well-from</code> flat to halfway, then to <code>--ai-well-to</code>. That's --color-lavender-50 to --color-lavender-400 on the default site, and the theme's 50 to 400 on themed pages (theme.css). Padding 1rem, radius lg.".html_safe do %>
      <div class="row g-4 align-items-start">
        <div class="col-lg-6">
          <div class="ai-well"><b>Suggested description</b><br>A gentle evening of breathwork and sound for all levels.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="col-lg-6">
          <div class="ask-box">
            <label class="visually-hidden" for="dg-ask">Ask a question</label>
            <textarea class="form-control autosize" id="dg-ask" rows="1" placeholder="Ask a question…"></textarea>
            <div class="ask-box-actions">
              <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary btn-sm" aria-label="Ask"><i class="bi bi-arrow-right" aria-hidden="true"></i></button>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>

  <!-- THEMING -->
  <% design_section 'theming', 'Organisations and events set one colour. <code>theme_css_variables</code> sets <code>--theme-500</code>, app.css derives the ramp from it, and every primary button, link, focus ring, crumb, check, progress bar, stats chart, alert and toast tint and date tile month follows. theme.css is only variables: as well as the theme colour, it switches the AI well to the theme ramp (see AI well and ask box), while the default site keeps it lavender as its own accent.'.html_safe do %>
    <div class="row g-3">
      <% ([[nil, nil]] + themed_colors).each do |color, clamped| %>
        <div class="col-md-6 col-xxl-4">
          <div class="<%= 'theme-scope' if color %> border rounded p-4 h-100 d-flex flex-column gap-3"<% if color %> style="<%= theme_css_variables(clamped).squish %>"<% end %>>
            <div class="spec fw-bold">
              <% if color %>
                THEMED · <%= color %><%= " → #{clamped} (clamped)" if clamped != color %>
              <% else %>
                DEFAULT · <span data-css-var="--theme-500"></span>
              <% end %>
            </div>
            <div class="d-flex flex-wrap gap-2 align-items-center">
              <a class="btn btn-primary" href="#theming">Book</a>
              <div class="nav-crumbs mb-0">
                <%= dropdown_nav [['Edit', '#theming']], button_text: 'Crumb' %>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="alert alert-primary mb-0">Saved. Text is --theme-800</div>
            <div class="ai-well">AI well: <%= color ? 'theme tint' : 'lavender' %></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    </div>
    <div class="small text-body-secondary">Each themed panel sets the same variables on itself that <code>/theme.css</code> sets on <code>:root</code>, from <code>theme_css_variables(clamp_color(colour))</code>, and has the <code>theme-scope</code> class so the ramp and focus ring are recomputed from its <code>--theme-500</code>.</div>
  <% end %>

</div>
<% end %>

<div class="design-layout">
  <nav id="design-nav" class="d-none d-lg-block" aria-label="Design guide">
    <nav class="nav flex-column">
      <% design_sections.each do |id, (title, _)| %>
        <a class="nav-link design-nav-section" href="#<%= id %>"><%= title %></a>
        <% if @design_toc[id].any? %>
          <nav class="nav flex-column">
            <% @design_toc[id].each do |subsection_id, subsection_title| %>
              <a class="nav-link" href="#<%= subsection_id %>"><%= subsection_title %></a>
            <% end %>
          </nav>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
    </nav>
  </nav>
  <%= guide %>
</div>

<script>
  $(function () {
    scrollspy('#design-nav a', '#design-nav');

    // Custom properties come back as written (e.g. oklch(from ...)), so paint each one to resolve it to hex
    var ctx = document.createElement('canvas').getContext('2d', { willReadFrequently: true });
    var probe = $('<span>').hide().appendTo('body')[0];
    $('[data-css-var]').each(function () {
      probe.style.color = 'var(' + $(this).attr('data-css-var') + ')';
      ctx.clearRect(0, 0, 1, 1);
      ctx.fillStyle = getComputedStyle(probe).color;
      ctx.fillRect(0, 0, 1, 1);
      var d = ctx.getImageData(0, 0, 1, 1).data;
      var hex = '#' + [0, 1, 2].map(function (i) { return d[i].toString(16).padStart(2, '0'); }).join('');
      $(this).text(d[3] < 255 ? hex + ' / ' + Math.round(d[3] / 2.55) + '%' : hex);
    });
    $('[data-css-value]').each(function () {
      $(this).text(getComputedStyle(document.documentElement).getPropertyValue($(this).attr('data-css-value')).trim());
    });
    $('[data-spec-row]').has('[data-sample]').each(function () {
      var px = parseFloat(getComputedStyle($(this).find('[data-sample]')[0]).fontSize);
      $(this).find('[data-px]').text(Math.round(px * 10) / 10 + 'px');
    });
    $('[data-space-sample]').each(function () {
      var px = parseFloat(getComputedStyle(this).height);
      $(this).closest('[data-spec-row]').find('[data-space-px]').text(Math.round(px * 10) / 10 + 'px');
    });
  });
</script>
